# data/ — the ONE canonical copy (read-only)

This is the project's **single source of experimental / reference data**, shared by every campaign and session
by **relative path** (`../../data`). This directory exists so the data is stored **once** — the duplication that
bloated prior investigations to hundreds of GB and broke a path on every move starts the moment a second copy is
made. Do not make one.

## Rules (non-negotiable)
1. **Read-only.** The loop **never writes into `data/`.** Derived/cached/generated data goes in the campaign's
   own `results/` or a campaign `cache/`, never here.
2. **Referenced, never copied.** Campaigns and sessions point at `../../data/<file>`. **Never copy the data into
   a campaign folder.** A copied dataset is what breaks paths on the next rename/move.
3. **Provenance recorded.** Each dataset's origin (instrument/run/date, or the external source) is documented —
   here or in `../shared/INSTRUMENT.md`.

## On-tree vs a `data_path` pointer
- **On-tree (default):** the read-only data files live right here in `data/`.
- **Off-tree pointer:** when the canonical data is large or already lives elsewhere (a lab store, a multi-hundred-GB
  pile), DON'T copy it in. Instead this directory holds a single pointer file **`DATA_PATH.txt`** whose one line
  is the **absolute path** to the real data root, and `PROJECT.md` records the same `data_path`. Code resolves
  `../../data` → that path once. **This is the only absolute path in the whole project tree** — everything else is
  relative, so the tree still relocates as one unit (only `DATA_PATH.txt` is re-pointed after a move of the data).

<!-- Off-tree example — the single line inside data/DATA_PATH.txt:
E:\canonical-store\asi-nv\D_experimental
